---
layout: layouts/product.njk
title: "Voice"
description: "Wholesale Voice Calling with origination, termination, VoiceML call control, STIR/SHAKEN, recordings, conferences, queues, and signed webhooks."
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}
{%- set years %}{% yearsSince 1999 %}{% endset %}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Service",
	"serviceType": "Wholesale voice origination and termination",
	"name": "VoiceTel Voice",
	"provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "{{ site.brand }}", "url": "{{ site.url }}" },
	"areaServed": ["US", "CA"],
	"url": "{{ site.url }}/voice/",
	"description": "Wholesale voice origination and termination with VoiceML call control, STIR/SHAKEN signing, Anycast and Geocast routing, diverse last-mile paths, recordings, conferences, queues, and signed webhooks."
}
</script>

{#- ───────────────────────── Hero ───────────────────────── -#}
<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Voice</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">Wholesale voice for managed service providers, carriers, and operators.</h1>
			<p class="lede">Fast, reliable, and uninterrupted voice delivery for business-critical traffic. Anycast, Geocast, and diverse last-mile routing keep call quality, continuity, and deliverability up under real-world conditions.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/pricing/#voice-out-us50">See pricing {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--secondary btn--lg" href="/voiceml/">Explore VoiceML</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set diagram = {
				title: "Voice path between the phone network and your PBX or application",
				nodes: [
					{ label: "PSTN", value: "Tier-1 carriers", icon: "telephone" },
					{ label: "VoiceTel POP", value: "STIR/SHAKEN signed", icon: "diagram-3", accent: true },
					{ label: "Your network", value: "PBX or app", meta: "SIP or VoiceML", icon: "buildings" }
				],
				links: [
					{ label: "Tier-1", both: true },
					{ label: "SIP trunk", both: true, accent: true }
				],
				meta: [
					{ k: "Routing", v: "Anycast · Geocast · diverse" },
					{ k: "Footprint", v: (site.pops | length) ~ " POPs · " ~ (site.cloudRegions | length) ~ " cloud regions" },
					{ k: "Direction", v: "inbound + outbound" }
				]
			} %}
			{% include "partials/v2/diagram.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

{#- ───────────────────────── Routing ───────────────────────── -#}
<section class="section section--tint" id="routing" aria-labelledby="routing-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">Routing</p>
				<h2 id="routing-heading">Anycast, Geocast, and diverse routing.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Outbound calls go to the nearest or best available node (Anycast) or to nodes in a specific region (Geocast). Inbound routing tests multiple paths and carriers and keeps the best one to the last hop.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/support/voice/sip-trunking/">SIP trunking guides</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set rows = [
					{ title: "Anycast", meta: "nearest or best available node", state: "Outbound", neutral: true },
					{ title: "Geocast", meta: "nodes in a specific region", state: "Outbound", neutral: true },
					{ title: "Diverse routing", meta: "best of several paths and carriers", state: "Inbound", neutral: true }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/status-card.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>

		<h3 class="subsection-heading">Voice capabilities</h3>
		{%- set featureHeading = "h4" %}
		{%- set features = [
			{ icon: "telephone", title: "Origination and termination", body: "Run inbound and outbound voice through VoiceTel with published rate keys, routing controls, and carrier-support escalation paths." },
			{ icon: "broadcast-pin", title: "Anycast", body: "Routes outbound traffic to the nearest or best available node among nodes advertising the same address, the pattern behind DNS, CDNs, and resilient network services." },
			{ icon: "geo-alt", title: "Geocast", body: "Routes outbound traffic to nodes within a specific geographic area, keeping media paths local for low latency and high call quality." },
			{ icon: "diagram-3", title: "Diverse routing", body: "Tests multiple network paths or carriers for inbound traffic, automatically selecting the best route and holding it stable to the last hop." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/feature-grid.njk" %}
	</div>
</section>

{#- ───────────────────────── Operational proof points ───────────────────────── -#}
<section class="section section--white" id="operations" aria-labelledby="operations-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">Operations</p>
			<h2 id="operations-heading">Signed calls, a published footprint, and operators who read SIP traces.</h2>
			<p class="lede">Caller identity and attestation on every call, network locations published on two continents, and escalations that reach people who can read SIP traces, carrier responses, and webhook logs.</p>
		</div>
		{%- set featureHeading = "h3" %}
		{%- set features = [
			{ icon: "shield-check", title: "STIR/SHAKEN aware", body: "Caller identity and attestation are part of the voice story, not an afterthought." },
			{ icon: "geo-alt", title: "Global colocation footprint", body: (site.pops | join(", ")) ~ ", plus " ~ (site.cloudRegions | join(", ")) ~ " cloud regions, are the published network locations.", href: "/infrastructure/", cta: "See the infrastructure" },
			{ icon: "headset", title: "Operator support", body: "Escalations reach people who can read SIP traces, carrier responses, and webhook logs.", href: "/support/", cta: "Open a ticket" }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/feature-grid.njk" %}
	</div>
</section>

{#- ───────────────────────── Compliance + closing CTA ───────────────────────── -#}
<section class="section section--tint" id="compliance" aria-labelledby="compliance-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row row--reverse">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">Compliance</p>
				<h2 id="compliance-heading">Fully licensed and compliant operations.</h2>
				<p class="lede">FCC-registered, operating as a CLEC, and listed in the Robocall Mitigation Database, with STIR/SHAKEN attestation on every call. Operating continuously since 1999 &mdash; {% yearsSince 1999 %} years in business, originally as an ISP, now a full-stack carrier.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/legal/">Legal and e911 notices</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set rows = [
					{ title: "FCC Form 499 filer", meta: "non-interconnected VoIP · ID 829231", state: "Registered" },
					{ title: "Robocall Mitigation Database", meta: "RMD0004909", state: "Registered" },
					{ title: "Competitive Local Exchange Carrier", meta: "OCN 470J", state: "Active" },
					{ title: "STIR/SHAKEN attestation", meta: "on every call", state: "Signed" },
					{ title: "In business since 1999", meta: "ISP roots · full-stack carrier", state: years ~ " yrs", neutral: true }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/status-card.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Send the first call.</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">Open an account and send us call traffic. If it doesn't outperform your current carrier, we'll want to see the trace.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signup/">Free trial {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/pricing/#voice-out-us50">See voice pricing</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
